---
description: Cross-cutting code quality, naming, isolation, and generation rules for the entire project.
alwaysApply: true
---

## Extend before creating
Reuse and extend existing repositories, clients, and providers before creating new files. Search the codebase first.

## Follow existing patterns exactly
When adding to a domain, mirror the naming, imports, and structure of the closest existing file in that layer. Do not introduce new naming conventions mid-project.

## No parallel implementations
Never duplicate logic across multiple files or layers. One canonical location per responsibility.

## Feature isolation
Features under `lib/src/` must not import from each other. If logic is needed across features, move it to `lib/data/` or `lib/utils/`.

## Use code generation — never hand-write generated shapes
- Models: use **Freezed** (`@freezed` + `part '*.freezed.dart'`, `part '*.g.dart'`).
- API clients: use **Retrofit** (`@RestApi`, `part '*.g.dart'`).
- Providers: use **Riverpod annotations** (`@riverpod`, `part '*.g.dart'`).

Never manually implement what code generation produces. Always run `dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs` after annotation changes.

## Naming must reflect layer

| Layer | Suffix / convention |
|---|---|
| Entry route widget | `*Page` class, `*_page.dart` file |
| Retrofit client class | `*Client`, file `*_client.dart` |
| Repository class | `*Repository`, file `*_repository.dart` |
| Provider file | `*_provider.dart` |
| Freezed model | `*Model`, file `*_model.dart` |

Avoid ambiguous names like `Manager`, `Handler`, `Helper`, `Controller` where a layer-specific name applies.

## No `print` statements
Use the centralized logger (`lib/logger/`) at boundaries. Use `debugPrint()` only for temporary local debugging that will be removed before committing.

## Log at boundaries
Log at:
- API call entry and response/error (client or repository layer).
- Navigation events (router layer).
- Unhandled errors and exception catches.

Do not log inside widgets or provider state reads.

## Enums
All shared enums must be defined in `lib/data/models/enums.dart`. Do not create enums inside feature folders, viewmodels, or services. Reuse existing enums before adding new ones.

## Money formatting
All monetary values must be formatted using `splitMoney(...)` from the local services layer. Never display raw numeric values for currency in the UI.

## No internal IDs in UI
Never display database or API IDs in widgets or labels. Use human-readable fields (name, title, code). If no display field exists, map to a UI-friendly value in the provider or repository.

## Directionality
UI direction is determined by the active app locale only (`MaterialApp` / `locale`). Never infer direction from text content. Do not wrap widgets with `Directionality` based on string language. Arabic = RTL, English = LTR.

## SVG icons first
Always check `assets/svg/` for a matching SVG asset before falling back to Flutter's `Icons` library.

## TextEditingController updates
Never assign `controller.text = ...` directly when the value comes from external state (sliders, providers, listeners, timers, async results). Always use the `setTextSafely(...)` extension from `lib/utils/extensions.dart`. Direct `.text =` leaves stale selection offsets and crashes on Android with `IndexOutOfBoundsException: invalid selection start` when the new text is shorter than the cached cursor position. The only acceptable raw `.text =` usage is initialization inside `useTextEditingController(text: ...)` or one-shot user-driven mutations where the field is unfocused and known empty.
